    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d200">

                <pb facs="0228" n="216" sameAs="frus:frus1940v03/pg216"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">861.011/51</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in the Soviet Union</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Thurston</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary
                        of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 726</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Moscow</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1940-09-04">September 4,
                        1940</date>.<lb/>[Received October 8.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to enclose herewith a
                    translation made in the Embassy of a law adopted on August 7, 1940, by the
                    Supreme Soviet of the U. S. S. R., which makes certain routine alterations in
                    the Constitution of the U. S. S. R., in connection with the organization of the
                    newly acquired territories of Bessarabia, Northern Bukovina, Lithuania, Latvia,
                    and Estonia.</p>
                <p>Respectfully yours,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Walter Thurston</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>


                <xi:include href="d200-a1.xml" xpointer="d200-a1"/>
            </div>
